# Copy to target.env (git-ignored) and set the real values for the e2e rig.
# Committed code and docs use placeholders only; the real gateway lives here.
#
# TJ_TEST_REF is the connect reference: a hostname or a tag such as tag:example.
# TJ_TEST_REMOTE is the gateway tailnet IPv4, for the SSH probe and the
# leftover-file check after the test.
TJ_TEST_REF=gw.example
TJ_TEST_REMOTE=100.64.0.10
TJ_TEST_USER=root
TJ_TEST_VPC_V4=10.0.0.0/16
TJ_TEST_VPC_V6=2001:db8::/56
TJ_TEST_RESOLVER=10.0.0.2
TJ_TEST_DNS_NAME=example.com
# Optional: an address outside the VPC that the gateway reaches over more than
# one hop, for the Time Exceeded check of traceroute. Leave it unset to skip.
# TJ_TEST_TRACE_TARGET=192.0.2.1
# Optional: a second remote in a private subnet that Tailscale relays through
# DERP, for the relayed-path scenario. Leave these unset to skip it.
# TJ_TEST_DERP_REF=relay.example
# TJ_TEST_DERP_REMOTE=100.64.0.11
# TJ_TEST_DERP_RESOLVER=10.1.0.2
# Optional: the tag of the gateways, and a second gateway that carries that
# tag, for the move scenario of reconnect.sh. The session follows the tag
# when the gateway it runs on leaves the tailnet. Leave these unset to skip
# that scenario.
# TJ_TEST_TAG=tag:example
# TJ_TEST_SECOND_REF=relay.example
# TJ_TEST_SECOND_REMOTE=100.64.0.11
